From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 20:27:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] feat(trace): Alt+T opens Trace Image for the selected
 image (ADR-396)

Alt+T (Option+T on macOS) opens Trace Image for the selected image, the
same as Tools > Trace Image and LightBurn's binding. Like the menu item it
does nothing unless the selected object is an image, and it waits while a
dialog, the canvas text editor or a text field has the keyboard. The
Tools menu and the top toolbar tooltip show Alt+T beside Trace Image,
the Keyboard Shortcuts list has a row for it, and the tracing lesson names
it.

On macOS the Option key types a character instead of the letter
(Option+T types a dagger, Option+M a micro sign), so the Alt chords now
fall back to the physical key when no plain letter was typed. Alt+M
(Measure) therefore starts working with Option+M too. AltGr, which
Windows reports as Ctrl+Alt, does not trigger either chord.

The Tools shortcut handler moved from shortcuts.ts, which was at the file
size limit, to tool-shortcuts.ts. The shortcut-list completeness test now
also expects Alt+T.

